ost 2109367628770746750</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2109367628770746750\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-10-11T19:36:47.000Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>thread</dt><dd>3027</dd><dt>thread_count</dt><dd>3031</dd><dt>conversation</dt><dd>1972960487148298273</dd>\n</dl>"},"2109379084962648273":{"a":"<p>So you&#x27;re telling me that after 40 years of digital government mandates  we haven&#x27;t digitized the laws we&#x27;re required to follow?</p>\n<p>I think there&#x27;s no reason to trust anything that tells you<br>\nthe proof your medicine is safe is<br>\nlocked in a filing cabinet under water guarded by lions. <a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2109379084962648273\">Tweet by @DavidLNorris</a></p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUYFGC2XQAAAdFR.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUYFGTiXQAAq3lH.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\" data-conversation=\"none\" data-dnt=\"true\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2109379084962648273\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2109379084962648273</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\" data-conversation=\"none\" data-dnt=\"true\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1971713802015236554\">https://x.com/i/status/1971713802015236554</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2109379084962648273</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2109379084962648273\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-10-11T20:22:18.000Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>thread</dt><dd>1192</dd><dt>thread_count</dt><dd>1491</dd><dt>conversation</dt><dd>1971623093094568310</dd>\n</dl>"},"2109401345648169021":{"a":"<p>Ham Spot Commander setup and tuning. Commander includes a meter panel which automatically populates with all of the instruments in the connected radio. Warning lights are Collins radio style from the 1960s with analog dials.</p>\n<p>If you are using a digital radio mode you might appreciate the dedicated named audio channels for the radios attached. You can select the auto created audio port from the input/output of your digital radio modem software.</p>\n<p>Commander automatically creates dedicated audio patch panels and ports as well as configuring serial connections for most devices. If you attach GQRX it prompts for IO Device config. Here you can attach your radio&#x27;s control channel and attach the demodulator to a pre-created audio patch port for this radio. This makes it easier to manage the audio connections, in theory. If you have complex audio routing this might prove useful. For example, an audio mixer panel connected via USB will show up here.</p>\n<p>When you close Commander everything it created will be torn down and saved into the station config (config tab press Save button; do this once to save your settings and patch cables) so they can be recreated exactly the same the next time this Station Config file is loaded.</p>\n<p>All of the other config files are embedded into the station config. That include GQRX and GPredict config files. Commander temporarily moves your existing config otu of the way while it is running and substitutes the embedded station config. (Sadly GUI authors often fail to include useful command line options. Some config files are hard coded into the software. I will eventually patch these apps to accept a config file on the command line. Sigh.)</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\" data-conversation=\"none\" data-dnt=\"true\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2109401345648169021\">View video on X</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\" data-conversation=\"none\" data-dnt=\"true\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2109401345648169021\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2109401345648169021</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-twe